  "instructionHtml": "<p>While validating an asynchronous KV connector, I captured the following scheduler state for a 70-token request:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki ai-infra-paper\" style=\"background-color:#F8F7F3;color:#303638\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>connector result: matched_tokens=37, load_kv_async=True</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>request state after scheduling: WAITING_FOR_REMOTE_KVS</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>runner input after transfer completion: num_computed_tokens=48</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>tokens scheduled after transfer completion: 22</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Where are the extra cached tokens coming from between the connector result and the runner input? Fix this so the two sides agree on how much of the request has already been computed, while behavior that already works correctly stays unchanged.</p>",
